From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:52:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] CandyOS P38: Settings dialogs and Material surfaces
 pinned dark

4.4 Settings was dark only; three surfaces still flipped light in
day mode through DayNight parents:

- Theme.AlertDialog.Base (the app's AndroidX alert dialog theme)
  was Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.Dialog.Alert with a surface_light
  background - every in-app dialog (Wi-Fi forget/edit, app info,
  reset confirmations) rendered light in day mode. Parented to the
  dark Theme.AppCompat.Dialog.Alert with the system_neutral1_800
  background, mirroring the SettingsLib 11.6 dialog fix; the
  accent stays accent_device_default_light (= Holo blue, the 4.4
  dialog button color).

- Theme.TabTheme and Theme.CollapsingToolbar.Settings were
  MaterialComponents.DayNight with light color pins (used by the
  preference_list_fragment TabLayout, request_manage_credentials
  and the dream preview button). Parented to the dark
  MaterialComponents base with the DeviceDefault dark pins.

The face-enroll accessibility toggle keeps its MaterialSwitch (no
4.4 counterpart - accepted per rule 5).

Change-Id: Ic1b2bfb240c0c20693ecead7237a279198ec4319
---
 res/values/themes.xml | 23 +++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/res/values/themes.xml b/res/values/themes.xml
index 1de867cb9bb..f768358810e 100644
--- a/res/values/themes.xml
+++ b/res/values/themes.xml
@@ -117,10 +117,15 @@
         <item name="android:windowSoftInputMode">adjustResize</item>
     </style>
 
-    <style name="Theme.AlertDialog.Base" parent="@style/Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.Dialog.Alert">
+    <!-- KitKat UI Project (P38): AppCompat DayNight resolves to the LIGHT
+         alert dialog in day mode; parented to the dark AppCompat dialog and
+         pinned to the SettingsLib dialog surface to match the forced-dark
+         Settings (mirrors the SettingsLib 11.6 fix). 4.4 dialogs were dark
+         only. -->
+    <style name="Theme.AlertDialog.Base" parent="@style/Theme.AppCompat.Dialog.Alert">
         <item name="colorAccent">@*android:color/accent_device_default_light</item>
         <item name="android:colorError">@color/settings_dialog_colorError</item>
-        <item name="android:colorBackground">@*android:color/surface_light</item>
+        <item name="android:colorBackground">@*android:color/system_neutral1_800</item>
     </style>
 
     <style name="Theme.AlertDialog" parent="Theme.AlertDialog.Base">
@@ -239,15 +244,17 @@
         <item name="notification_importance_button_foreground_color_selected">@android:color/system_on_secondary_container_light</item>
     </style>
 
-    <!-- Material theme for the pages containing TabLayout and ViewPager -->
-    <style name="Theme.TabTheme" parent="@style/Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight">
-        <item name="colorPrimary">@*android:color/edge_effect_device_default_light</item>
+    <!-- KitKat UI Project (P38): TabLayout/ViewPager and collapsing-toolbar
+         pages parented to the dark MaterialComponents base (DayNight
+         rendered them light in day mode; 4.4 Settings was dark only). -->
+    <style name="Theme.TabTheme" parent="@style/Theme.MaterialComponents">
+        <item name="colorPrimary">@*android:color/edge_effect_device_default_dark</item>
     </style>
 
-    <style name="Theme.CollapsingToolbar.Settings" parent="@style/Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight">
+    <style name="Theme.CollapsingToolbar.Settings" parent="@style/Theme.MaterialComponents">
         <item name="elevationOverlayEnabled">true</item>
         <item name="elevationOverlayColor">?attr/colorPrimary</item>
-        <item name="colorPrimary">@*android:color/primary_device_default_settings_light</item>
-        <item name="colorAccent">@*android:color/accent_device_default_light</item>
+        <item name="colorPrimary">@*android:color/primary_dark_device_default_settings</item>
+        <item name="colorAccent">@*android:color/accent_device_default_dark</item>
     </style>
 </resources>
